[36m(RewardLoopWorker pid=18188)[0m Last Man Standing is an American teen sitcom that premiered on March 23, 2011, on the ABC network. The show centers around father-son dad and son characters Carter Bailey (Drew Titus) and Kyle Anderson (Christoph Sanders), the latter of whom is a firefighter who works for the Jonah Firehouse. The series is notable for its almost documentary-style nature. The show was created by Greg Daniels and is based on a short film about families that Daniels wrote for the TV show "". ABC Family dropped the show in 2013, citing ratings of 1.63 million, a number that followed the show 11.7 million during the first three seasons. In September 2013, the show was ordered by ABC to be re-named ""Last Man Standing"" and air on ABC as a regular sitcom. The first thirty-somes in The Jonas Family were conceived in August 2000 when series creator Greg Daniels wrote a short film about a father and son family as a potential pilot idea. A fake pilot was created and filmed for ABC TV in April 2001 and received a mostly positive response from the network's creative department. HBO picked up the short film as a pilot and based a 30 minute TV series on it. It ran on HBO Family from October 21, 2002 - June 20, 2006. A series of unique commercials for the TV series were also aired. The show, A Story of Two Families, was later shown on YouTube in July 2008. In February 2013, television producer James Burrows commented to the Associated Press that he thought the show was four seasons behind.
